{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having trouble swallowing and throat pain since your tracheostomy was upsized?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started three days ago. It hurts to swallow and I feel like I might choke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned increased secretions too. Any fever, shortness of breath, or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or trouble breathing. Just pain and fear of choking. I haven’t eaten much in three days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll keep you NPO for now and give IV fluids. We’ll also check your airway to make sure everything’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll likely do a bronchoscopy to look at your airway. It’s common to have swelling after trach changes. We just want to make sure it’s not blocking your swallowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. It usually gets better in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s consistent with what we see. Post-op swelling is expected. We’ll manage your pain and monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have something for the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll give you IV morphine for now. Once you can eat, we’ll switch to liquid Tylenol with codeine, which you used at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-09-28 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-09-28 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray came back normal. No pneumonia or aspiration. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-09-28 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Is my trach site okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-09-28 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, minimal redness, no infection. We’ll keep it clean and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did the bronchoscopy yesterday. There’s severe swelling in the supraglottic area, which explains your pain and swallowing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your airway is safe. The swelling is expected after the procedure. ENT also scoped you and confirmed scarring and vocal fold fixation, but nothing urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it should get better on its own?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with time and pain control. We’re starting your home meds again—Montelukast, albuterol nebs as needed, and omeprazole for reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my fluoxetine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-09-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held it while you were NPO, but now that you’re stable, we’ll restart it with your meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-09-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The speech team did a swallowing study. You tolerated thin liquids and regular food without aspiration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-09-30 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Even though I felt like I was choking on the cracker?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-09-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that sensation is common with your anatomy. But the study showed no residue or penetration. You’re safe to eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-09-30 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I start eating now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-09-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on a regular diet. Let us know if you have any discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I ate some soup and crackers. It felt better than yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Your pain is improving too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, much less pain. I think I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. We’ll switch your pain med to liquid Tylenol with codeine for home use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need to follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with your surgeon in one week and your primary care doctor. We’re not changing any of your regular medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my albuterol and reflux meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-09-30 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue exactly as before—albuterol nebs as needed, omeprazole twice daily, and ranitidine at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-10-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re finalizing your discharge. You’re doing well—eating, pain controlled, no breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-10-01 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-10-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home with instructions and your pain med. Call your surgeon if pain worsens or you have trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-10-01 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I have my follow-up scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-10-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re cleared to go home today. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-09-28 13:25:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-10-01 12:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia and tracheostomy status was admitted for dysphagia and severe odynophagia following a recent tracheostomy upsizing procedure. She had been unable to tolerate oral intake for three days due to fear of choking and throat pain. Evaluation revealed no signs of infection or respiratory distress. Bronchoscopy showed severe supraglottic edema, and ENT evaluation confirmed scarring and vocal fold fixation consistent with postoperative changes. A videofluoroscopic swallow study demonstrated safe swallowing with thin liquids and regular solids, despite the patient's sensation of choking. Pain was managed with IV morphine initially, then transitioned to oral Tylenol with codeine. Her home medications for asthma, GERD, and depression were resumed. She improved steadily, resumed a regular diet, and was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up planned with her surgeon and primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Edema of larynx",
      "Other anomalies of larynx, trachea, and bronchus",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Dysphagia, oropharyngeal phase",
      "Other acute postoperative pain",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
